<title>USA: NationsBank sees rising savings in merger.</title>
<headline>NationsBank sees rising savings in merger.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NationsBank Corp said annual savings in its planned merger with Boatmen's Bancshares Inc will be $140 million in 1997, and then rise to $295 million in 1998 and to $335 million in 1999.</p>
<p>A spokesman said the $335 million in annual savings would continue each year after 1999.</p>
<p>The merger, which is expected to close in January, 1997, is subject to approval of shareholders of both companies and also needs regulatory approval.</p>
<p>NationsBank was off 7-3/8 to 85 and Boatmen's was up 10-13/16 to 53-3/4 in late morning.</p>
</text>
